<p>
  The main components of the App are <strong>Issues</strong> and <strong>Tasks</strong>.
  Issues are similar to GitHub issues. Anyone with access can use them to report bugs,
  suggest improvements, or ask a question. On the other hand, tasks can only be created by
  <strong>Reviewers</strong> or <strong>Admins</strong>. Often times, they are created
  from an Issue. They lay out specific instructions on how to fix the Issues' bugs or
  complete new features. Tasks can also be added independently.
</p>

<h3>Type Configuration</h3>
<p>
  Issues and Tasks are grouped by <strong>types</strong> (eg. Bug, Feature Request,
  Question). There are several color and icon options available that can be used in order
  to customize their tags:
</p>

<h4>Color and Icon Options</h4>
<div class="issue-tags">
  <%= type_color_options %>
</div>

<h4>Icon Options</h4>
<div class="issue-tags">
  <%= type_icon_options %>
</div>

<h3>Categories and Projects</h3>
<p>
  Issues and Tasks are added to <strong>Projects</strong>, which are added to
  <strong>Categories</strong>. Each can be set as <strong>Internal</strong> which hides
  the Category/Project and it's underlying Issues and Tasks from
  <strong>Reporters</strong>. In addition, each can be set as <strong>Archived</strong>.
  This hides the Category/Project from <strong>Workers</strong> and
  <strong>Reporters</strong> and prevents new Issues/Tasks from being created within or
  even worked on.
</p>

<h3>Priority Levels</h3>
<p>
  Tasks have a priority level assigned to them that indicate the importance of the bug
  fix, improvement, or new feature. The options are 1 to 4. Here is the quick guide
  of the levels and how they can be used:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong class="color-red">Critical</strong> - Most likely tied to a bug that effects many users or clients</li>
  <li><strong class="color-yellow">High</strong> - An important bug fix or new improvement</li>
  <li><strong class="color-purple">Medium</strong> - A new feature or improvement</li>
  <li><strong class="color-blue">Low</strong> - A new feature or improvement that can wait</li>
</ol>

<h3>Subscriptions</h3>
<p>
  Issues and Tasks can be subscribed to. Afterwords, users will receive notifications
  when the status changes or comments are added. Furthermore, users can auto-subscribe to
  Issues and Tasks based on search filters (eg. Project, Issue/Task Type, Status, User).
</p>
